tei:div.tei:p:
My beloved called and said to me: “Rise, my love, my beauty, come away. 

For, lo, the winter is over, the rain is past and gone; 

the flowers appear on the earth, the time of song has come; and the call of the turtle-dove is heard in our land; 

the fig-tree is ripening its early figs, and the vines in blossom give forth their fragrance. Rise, my love, my beauty, come away. 

O my dove, in the clefts of the rock, in the covert of the cliff, let me see your form, let me hear your voice; for sweet is your voice, and your form is comely.”
